  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 200°C and line a tagine pot with parchment paper.",
    "Sift together quinoa flour, all‑purpose flour, baking powder, salt, pepper, and dried dill in a bowl.",
    "Whisk plant‑based butter, oat milk, and maple syrup until the butter is fully incorporated.",
    "Add the wet mixture to the dry ingredients and stir until just combined.",
    "Shape the dough into small rounds and place them in the prepared tagine pot.",
    "Roast in the oven for 15 minutes until golden and slightly puffed.",
    "Remove the scones and let them cool for 5 minutes.",
    "Serve each scone with a dollop of cashew cream drizzled on top.",
    "Enjoy your nourishing British quinoa scones."
